This Sooty_Mould `Mango_Leaf_288.jpg` image has dark spots but they are more uniformly black and scattered, whereas the test image has more irregular, brownish lesions, often coalescing at the edges of the leaf.

Based on the visual comparisons, the Anthracnose reference image `Mango_Leaf_383.jpg` is the most similar to the test image. The irregular brown spots and their distribution closely match.

{"prediction": "Anthracnose", "confidence": 0.9, "reasoning": "The test image shows irregular brown lesions on a mango leaf. The reference image for Anthracnose (Mango_Leaf_383.jpg) exhibits very similar irregular, dark brown to black spots on a green leaf, matching the visual characteristics and distribution in the test image more closely than any other class. While the test image's spots are slightly lighter brown, the overall pattern is a strong match. Other classes like Die_Back and Powdery_Mildew present entirely different symptoms (dried shriveled leaves or white powdery growth, respectively). Sooty_Mould images show more uniform dark, sooty coatings rather than distinct brown spots."}
